<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Mud Creek Ridge and Porcupine Trail (from Trillium Lake Sno-Park)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:143-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.285259" lon="-121.727970"><ele>1156.8</ele><name>Trillium Lake Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:trillium-lake-sno-park (OSM parking way/148019331); confidence: high; pdf_page: 143; book_elev_ft: 3830</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.280208" lon="-121.733236"><ele>1103.1</ele><name>Airstrip junction</name><desc>source: as in or-vielbig-2e_147-4; confidence: high; pdf_page: 144</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.270371" lon="-121.732742"><ele>1103.9</ele><name>Campground junction</name><desc>source: as in or-vielbig-2e_147-4: OSM node 37397443, north end of the Trillium Lake Loop Road (NF 2656); confidence: high; pdf_page: 146; quote: From the campground junction east of Trillium Lake (see map) take the road angling uphill</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.247584" lon="-121.738954"><ele>1191.7</ele><name>Jefferson Viewpoint</name><desc>source: as in or-vielbig-2e_147-4: OSM node 37598733, the sweeping turn of NF 2656; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 146; book_elev_ft: 3940; quote: a long, gentle climb to the Jefferson Viewpoint, 1.8 miles from the junction and 3.5 miles from the sno-park</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.247610" lon="-121.736610"><ele>1193.2</ele><name>Porcupine Trail start</name><desc>source: OSM node 37274324: where the unnamed TIGER track way 5273549 (USFS roads 2656130/2656080 start here too) leaves NF 2656 to the north, 0.13 mi east of the viewpoint; map 33 draws the trail leaving the road just east of the viewpoint, west of the Salmon River Overlook; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 146; quote: Follow the road as it curves eastward. Where it starts to curve southward, leave the road and enter a large clearcut to the north, following a primitive road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.258470" lon="-121.725210"><ele>1200.5</ele><name>Porcupine Trail end (final clearcut)</name><desc>source: North end of OSM track way 5273549 (node 37274423), on the east side of Mud Creek Ridge; map 33 draws the trail ending in a clearcut north of the 4150' spot; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 148; quote: After entering the forest, climb in a northerly direction along the side of Mud Creek Ridge, then descend into a final clearcut.</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Mud Creek Ridge and Porcupine Trail (from Trillium Lake Sno-Park)</name><desc>1. Trillium Lake Sno-Park -&gt; Airstrip junction: osm (high), 0.48 mi | 2. Airstrip junction -&gt; Campground junction: osm (high), 0.84 mi | 3. Campground junction -&gt; Jefferson Viewpoint: osm (high), 1.76 mi | 4. Jefferson Viewpoint -&gt; Porcupine Trail start: osm (high), 0.12 mi | 5. Porcupine Trail start -&gt; Porcupine Trail end (final clearcut): osm (medium), 1.14 mi</desc>
